            <ArticleTitle>Influence of hydrochlorothiazide on the pain threshold and on the antinociceptive activity of morphine, in rats.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>265-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Hydrochlorothiazide, acutely injected in rats, has a weak analgesic activity per se and potentiates and prolongs the antinociceptive effect of morphine.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
